    #  DJ. After the plants, the main tree's xml tests (features off) and copy
    #      tests (copy with comments) run again, the same names as before them
    #      (ruling 10's control, as P3's change LM; the tool's copy sample
    #      tests are no longer named, since P4 adds no tool test).
    #  DK. The status patterns name this phase's log directory, its record stems
    #      records/m3p6-p4-, records/m3p6-open- and records/size-m3p6-, and
    #      planning's specs/0028, each with a control.
    #  DL. Ruling 10 carried: the phase's target root <phase>/target, written
    #      <target>, now P4's; <target>/main for <repo>, <target>/plant for the
    #      plants.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 7 P2 from M3 part 6 P4's test script (at the phase
    # commit 9cfd92e, printed in records/logs/m3p6-p4/test.log; its change list
    # DA to DL is above), generated by
    # <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p2/gen/test.py, which asserts each
    # replacement's count, and grepped for P4's subjects, hashes, roles, tests
    # and plants over the body. M3 part 7 P1's test log ran no crate test (P1
    # changed scripts only), so P4's is the frame. What differs, and why:
    #  FA. The phase is Milestone 3 part 7 P2: records/logs/m3p7-p2; the script
    #      on the disk in <scripts>, its stderr in <phase>/out. The base is P1's
    #      record commit ("M3 part 7 P1 record:"); the doc commit and the one
    #      code commit, the phase commit, by their full subjects, beginning "M3
    #      part 7 P2: ", the roles read back to <phase commit>~2. The previous
    #      phase's names and total are read from records/logs/m3p6-p4/test.log,
    #      the last test log with crate runs before the base (P1's ran none and
    #      changed no test). Every rm -rf is on a directory this run made,
    #      written with ${var:?}.
    #  FB. The spec is specs/0029, pinned by its COMMITTED blob (639b630c...,
    #      the hash planning's brief gave for the doc commit), at the phase
    #      commit; the control refuses specs/0028's blob at the phase commit.
    #      The working tree's copy is printed, not pinned; the entry guard and
    #      the status block allow this phase's log directory and ` M
    #      specs/0029-...` alone (the phase writes no record).
    #  FC. The crate's own runs as P4's: the features off, copy alone, comments
    #      alone and copy with comments, on both targets, and every feature on
    #      the host and on i686.
    #  FD. The tests the source adds, derived from the diff: no test file is
    #      new; the code commit adds one test to package/tests/copy.rs, the one
    #      its message names, and no other file gains a test.
    #  FE. In place of P4's Scope test: the new test runs and passes in the two
    #      sets with copy on both targets and in neither without, and in both
    #      runs with every feature.
    #  FF. In place of P4's two alone runs: the new test run alone with copy
    #      alone; it is absent from the run with the features off.
    #  FG. specs/0029 item 6, "the full copy test's bytes do not move": the full
    #      copy test a_copy_keeps_the_sheet_and_leaves_out_what_it_does_not_carry
    #      run alone with copy alone, the base holding it by name, and its two
    #      literals, FULL_BODY (the source) and FULL_COPIED (what the copy
    #      writes), each read from copy.rs by git show at the base and at the
    #      phase commit (from its `const` line through the first line ending
    #      `";`) and hashed: equal at both commits, with a control that the two
    #      literals differ from each other and that a name the file lacks reads
