    #  FH. The calcPr block's control: a test the base lacks, the code commit's
    #      new test (P4's control named P4's copy test, which the base now holds).
    #  FI. The plants: P4's D plants are dropped (their code is P4's and
    #      unchanged). Two rows on the code commit's two calls in
    #      crates/emend/src/package.rs, each removing one call: L1 the
    #      sheetView branch's, L2 the sheetPr branch's, each against the new
    #      test with copy alone. Both fail at the test's one refusal line (its
    #      refused_with call, inside the loop over the two bodies; refused_with
    #      and refused carry #[track_caller]), so the lines are not distinct;
    #      the two panic messages, which name the bytes the unrefused write
    #      wrote, are printed and checked to differ. After the plants the main
    #      tree's copy tests (copy with comments) pass, the same names as before
    #      them, the new test among them.
    #  FJ. The status patterns name this phase's log directory and planning's
    #      specs/0029, each with a control.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 7 P3 from M3 part 7 P2's test script (at the phase
    # commit 8d54741, printed in records/logs/m3p7-p2/test.log; its change list
    # FA to FJ is above), generated by
    # <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p3/gen/test.py, which asserts each
    # replacement's count, and grepped for P2's subjects, hashes, tests, plants
    # and crate runs over the body. P3 changes no Rust source: the crate's tests
    # run in the gate log, so this log runs none. What differs, and why:
    #  GA. The phase is Milestone 3 part 7 P3: records/logs/m3p7-p3; the script
    #      on the disk in <scripts>, its stderr in <phase>/out. The base is P2's
    #      record commit ("M3 part 7 P2 record:"); the doc commit, the rules
    #      commit (specs/0001's toolchain-pin bullet, a doc-only commit by the
    #      implementing session) and the code commit, the phase commit, by
    #      their full subjects, beginning "M3 part 7 P3: ", the roles read back
    #      to <phase commit>~3. The one build is the doc build, into
    #      <target>/main. Every rm -rf is on a directory this run made, written
    #      with ${var:?}.
    #  GB. The spec is specs/0029, pinned by its COMMITTED blob (7005aa50...,
    #      the hash planning's brief gave for the doc commit), at the phase
    #      commit; the control refuses specs/0028's blob at the phase commit.
    #  GC. T1, the pub listing (specs/0029 "The API review (decision 3)", A):
    #      the program <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p3/gen/api-listing.py,
    #      inserted whole into this script, written to <scratch>/w/py and run
